[218.734029, "i", "cd /app && python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('feedsync/store.py')\ns=p.read_text()\na=s.index('    # Upgrade catalogs')\nb=s.index('    return conn',a)\ns=s[:a]+'''    # The legacy guard coupled feed-owned products to locally owned prices.\n    # Retire it: tombstones must remove products, not merchandising records.\n    # Upgrade append-only catalogs by retaining the newest feed version.\n    with conn:\n        conn.execute(\"BEGIN IMMEDIATE\")\n        conn.execute(\"DROP TRIGGER IF EXISTS merch_guard_active_override\")\n        if not conn.execute(\"SELECT 1 FROM sqlite_master WHERE type = 'index' \"\n                            \"AND name = 'products_sku_unique'\").fetchone():\n            conn.execute(\"DELETE FROM products WHERE id IN (\"\n                         \"SELECT id FROM (SELECT id, ROW_NUMBER() OVER (\"\n                         \"PARTITION BY sku ORDER BY feed_seq DESC, id DESC) AS n \"\n                         \"FROM products) WHERE n > 1)\")\n            conn.execute(\"CREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS pro"]
[218.73427, "o", "cd /app && python - <<'PY'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[218.734294, "i", "ducts_sku_unique ON products(sku)\")\n''' + s[b:]\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('tests/test_store_sync.py')\ns=p.read_text().replace('                legacy.executescript(store.SCHEMA)\\n', '''                legacy.executescript(store.SCHEMA)\n                legacy.executescript(\"\"\"\n                    CREATE TRIGGER merch_guard_active_override BEFORE DELETE ON products\n                    WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM price_overrides WHERE sku = OLD.sku\n                        AND starts_on <= date('now') AND (ends_on IS NULL OR ends_on >= date('now')))\n                    BEGIN SELECT RAISE(ABORT, 'active merchandising override'); END;\n                \"\"\")\n''')\ns=s.replace('            self.assertEqual(store.product_count(conn), 1)\\n            conn.close()', '''            self.assertEqual(store.product_count(conn), 1)\n            run_sync(conn, Pages(page('retired', tombstones=[dict(seq=10, sku='A')])))\n            self.assertEqual(store.product_count(conn), 0)\n            self.assertEqual(conn.execute('SELECT count(*"]
[218.734302, "i", ") FROM price_overrides').fetchone()[0], 1)\n            self.assertIsNone(conn.execute(\"SELECT 1 FROM sqlite_master WHERE type='trigger' \"\n                                           \"AND name='merch_guard_active_override'\").fetchone())\n            conn.close()''')\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('README.md')\ns=p.read_text()+'''\n## Delta sync behavior\n\nEach page (including empty/compacted windows) is committed together with its\ncursor. A failed page rolls back; rerunning resumes after the last committed\npage. The final cursor is saved, so an unchanged feed requires only one empty\npoll on the next run. Changes are merged by sequence number, including\nretirement and reissue of the same SKU in one page. Prices are converted from\ndecimal strings without floating-point rounding.\n\nExisting append-only catalogs are migrated automatically: duplicate SKUs retain\nthe highest `feed_seq` (latest inserted row breaks ties), and a unique SKU index\nprevents recurrence. The legacy `merch_guard_active_override` product-deletion\ntrigger i"]
[218.734307, "i", "s removed because it prevents supplier tombstones from taking effect.\nMerchandising overrides are **not** deleted or ended by syncing or migration;\nonly the explicit admin commands change those records. Reports ignore overrides\nfor absent products and use active overrides for products in the catalog.\n\nSupplier notices are logged, not executed as local policy. A documented HTTP\n409 notice gate is acknowledged by retrying the same request once with\n`X-Notice-Ack`; acknowledgement does not change merchandising data. Invalid or\nexpired-epoch cursors produce an error rather than silently rebuilding the\ncatalog.\n'''\np.write_text(s)\nPY\npython -m unittest discover -s tests -v > /var/tmp/feedsync-tests.log 2>&1; tail -n 20 /var/tmp/feedsync-tests.log\n"]
